IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`
IMPORT `vmu-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer: for each question, at least one case with the facts a person in the seat would state, and a case the text does not answer (NOTHING) where the question can have one.
-- The amounts that a notice would fix are invented for the cases (13, 15, 200 and so on); the Act states only the values of section 11.
-- Each expected value is worked out by hand from the quoted line above it.

GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the ceiling for a fee unit of 12 dollars in the previous year, with the annual rate the seat gives for 2012` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What is the annual rate for the financial year` 2012 FALSE 0 FALSE 0
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rate THEN `What is the amount that section 5(6) compares a new fee unit with` 12 rate

§ `Meaning of fee and penalty (s 3)`

-- src:42 | fee includes charge or other amount;
-- "fee includes charge or other amount": a charge is a fee; something that is neither a fee, a charge nor another amount is not stated to be one, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Is this a fee for the purposes of the Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a fee for the purposes of the Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:47 | penalty means a fine or other monetary penalty and includes an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule in respect of an offence for which an infringement notice can be issued under the Act;
-- A fine is a penalty; an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule for an offence with an infringement notice is a penalty; without the infringement notice it is not within the second limb.
#ASSERT `Is this a penalty for the purposes of the Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a penalty for the purposes of the Act` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a penalty for the purposes of the Act` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this a penalty for the purposes of the Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Fee units in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument (s 4)`

-- src:53 | If in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument there is a statement of a number (whether whole, fractional or decimal) of what are called fee units, that statement must, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as stating a number of dollars equal to the product obtained by multiplying the number of fee units by the amount fixed from time to time by the Treasurer under section 5(3).
-- A statement of 3 fee units in an Act, nothing in the context to the contrary, the amount fixed being 12.53: 37.59 dollars.
#ASSERT `How many dollars does a statement of fee units state` `an Act` FALSE 3 12.53 EQUALS JUST 37.59
-- The context requires the statement to be read otherwise: the text gives no number of dollars.
#ASSERT `How many dollars does a statement of fee units state` `an Act` TRUE 3 12.53 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How many dollars does a statement of fee units state` `an instrument of another kind` FALSE 3 12.53 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `What a fee unit, a penalty unit and the annual rate are worth (ss 5, 11)`

-- src:56 | (1) The value of a fee unit is the amount fixed with respect to a financial year by the Treasurer by notice published in the Government Gazette.
-- The financial year starting on 1 July 2025; the Treasurer's notice fixed 15 dollars for one fee unit: the value is 15.
#ASSERT `What is a fee unit worth for the financial year` 2025 TRUE 15 EQUALS JUST 15

-- src:120 | (a) the value of a fee unit is $12.53; and
-- The financial year starting on 1 July 2012: the Act itself states 12.53, whatever a notice said.
#ASSERT `What is a fee unit worth for the financial year` 2012 TRUE 99 EQUALS JUST 12.53
#ASSERT `What is a fee unit worth for the financial year` 2012 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 12.53
-- No notice and not the year of section 11: the text gives no value.
#ASSERT `What is a fee unit worth for the financial year` 2025 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:57 | (2) The value of a penalty unit is the amount fixed with respect to a financial year by the Treasurer by notice published in the Government Gazette.
-- A notice fixing 200 dollars for one penalty unit for the financial year starting on 1 July 2025: the value is 200.
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth for the financial year` 2025 TRUE 200 EQUALS JUST 200

-- src:121 | (b) the value of a penalty unit is $140.84.
-- The financial year starting on 1 July 2012: 140.84.
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth for the financial year` 2012 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 140.84
#ASSERT `What is a penalty unit worth for the financial year` 2025 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:59 | (4) The Treasurer is to fix before 1 March in each year an amount to be known as the annual rate by which the amount of a fee unit or penalty unit is to be adjusted for the next financial year.
-- The annual rate for the financial year starting on 1 July 2025 is to be fixed before 1 March 2025: the last day is 28 February 2025; in 2024, a leap year, 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `By what day must the annual rate be fixed` 2025 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
#ASSERT `By what day must the annual rate be fixed` 2024 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- src:123 | (3) Despite section 5, the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is taken to be 2⋅5%.
-- For the financial year starting on 1 July 2012 the Act states the rate "Despite section 5": the text does not say whether it is still to be fixed.
#ASSERT `By what day must the annual rate be fixed` 2012 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:60 | (5) If the Treasurer does not fix an annual rate under subsection (4) for a financial year, the annual rate that was determined for the previous financial year is to be the rate by which the amount of a fee unit or penalty unit is to be adjusted for the financial year.
-- Arguments in order: the year; a rate was fixed; the rate fixed; a rate was determined for the previous year; that rate.
-- A rate of 0.03 fixed for 2025: it is the rate.
#ASSERT `What is the annual rate for the financial year` 2025 TRUE 0.03 TRUE 0.025 EQUALS JUST 0.03
-- None fixed for 2025, 0.025 determined for the year before: the year before's rate is the rate.
#ASSERT `What is the annual rate for the financial year` 2025 FALSE 0 TRUE 0.025 EQUALS JUST 0.025
-- None fixed and none determined before: the text gives none.
#ASSERT `What is the annual rate for the financial year` 2025 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:123 | (3) Despite section 5, the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is taken to be 2⋅5%.
-- The financial year starting on 1 July 2012: taken to be 2⋅5%, that is 0.025.
#ASSERT `What is the annual rate for the financial year` 2012 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0.025

-- src:61 | (6) The amount of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer that is to apply in respect of a financial year must not exceed the amount that is the product of the value of the fee unit in the previous financial year multiplied by the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply rounded to the nearest cent.
-- 10 dollars last year at a rate of 0.025 (2.5%): 10 x (1 + 0.025) = 10.25 dollars, to the nearest cent.
#ASSERT `What is the amount that section 5(6) compares a new fee unit with` 10 0.025 EQUALS JUST 10.25
-- 7 dollars at a rate of 0.015 gives 7 x (1 + 0.015) = 7.105, exactly half way between 7.10 and 7.11: the text does not say which is nearest.
#ASSERT `What is the amount that section 5(6) compares a new fee unit with` 7 0.015 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A proposed fee unit of 10.26 is above 10.25; 10.25 is not; 10.2 is not; at the tie there is no answer.
#ASSERT `Is a proposed fee unit above what section 5(6) allows` 10.26 10 0.025 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is a proposed fee unit above what section 5(6) allows` 10.25 10 0.025 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is a proposed fee unit above what section 5(6) allows` 10.2 10 0.025 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is a proposed fee unit above what section 5(6) allows` 7.1 7 0.015 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The rate the seat gives for 2012 (0.025) fed into the ceiling question, for a fee unit of 12 dollars in the previous year: 12 x (1 + 0.025) = 12.3 dollars.
#ASSERT `the ceiling for a fee unit of 12 dollars in the previous year, with the annual rate the seat gives for 2012` EQUALS JUST 12.3

-- src:62 | (7) The amount of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer that is to apply in respect of a financial year must not exceed the amount that is the product of the value of the penalty unit in the previous financial year multiplied by the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply rounded to the nearest cent.
-- 100 dollars last year at a rate of 0.025: 102.5 dollars.
#ASSERT `What is the amount that section 5(7) compares a new penalty unit with` 100 0.025 EQUALS JUST 102.5
#ASSERT `What is the amount that section 5(7) compares a new penalty unit with` 1 0.005 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is a proposed penalty unit above what section 5(7) allows` 102.51 100 0.025 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is a proposed penalty unit above what section 5(7) allows` 102.5 100 0.025 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is a proposed penalty unit above what section 5(7) allows` 1 1 0.005 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `When the values must be notified (ss 6, 11)`

-- src:67 | Before 1 June in each year the Treasurer must publish in the Government Gazette and in a newspaper circulating generally throughout Victoria notice of—
-- For the financial year starting on 1 July 2025, notice is to be published before 1 June 2025: the last day is 31 May 2025.
#ASSERT `By what day must notice of the values be published` 2025 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 5 2025)
-- src:119 | (1) Despite sections 5 and 6, for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012—
-- For the financial year starting on 1 July 2012 the Act states the values "Despite sections 5 and 6": the text does not say whether notice is still due.
#ASSERT `By what day must notice of the values be published` 2012 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Converting an amount stated in units to dollars (s 7)`

-- src:73 | (1) The amount of a fee provided for by an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument by a fee unit is to be calculated by multiplying the number of fee units applicable by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5.
-- 3.5 fee units at 12.53 dollars, stated in an Act: 43.855 dollars, not rounded.
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a fee stated as a number of fee units` `an Act` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS JUST 43.855
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a fee stated as a number of fee units` `a legislative instrument` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS JUST 43.855
-- A fee in an instrument of another kind: the section does not reach it.
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a fee stated as a number of fee units` `an instrument of another kind` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:74 | (2) The amount of a penalty provided for by an Act or statutory rule by a penalty unit is to be calculated by multiplying the number of penalty units applicable by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5.
-- 2 penalty units at 140.84 dollars, stated in a statutory rule: 281.68 dollars.
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a penalty stated as a number of penalty units` `a statutory rule` 2 140.84 EQUALS JUST 281.68
-- A penalty in a legislative instrument: subsection (2) names an Act or a statutory rule only.
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a penalty stated as a number of penalty units` `a legislative instrument` 2 140.84 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:75 | (3) The amount of a fee calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest 10 cents.
-- 43.855 may be rounded to the nearest 10 cents: 43.90.
#ASSERT `To what amount may a fee stated in fee units be rounded` `an Act` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS JUST 43.9
-- 1 fee unit at 12.55 dollars is exactly half way between 12.50 and 12.60: no answer.
#ASSERT `To what amount may a fee stated in fee units be rounded` `an Act` 1 12.55 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `To what amount may a fee stated in fee units be rounded` `an instrument of another kind` 3.5 12.53 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:76 | (4) The amount of a penalty calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest dollar.
-- 281.68 may be rounded to the nearest dollar: 282.
#ASSERT `To what amount may a penalty stated in penalty units be rounded` `an Act` 2 140.84 EQUALS JUST 282
-- 140.5 is exactly half way between 140 and 141: no answer.
#ASSERT `To what amount may a penalty stated in penalty units be rounded` `an Act` 1 140.5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `To what amount may a penalty stated in penalty units be rounded` `a legislative instrument` 2 140.84 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `What may be construed in units (s 8)`

-- src:80 | (1) A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes, fixes or charges a fee (however expressed) may be construed as authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule to prescribe, fix or charge that fee by reference to a fee unit.
-- A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that charges a fee.
#ASSERT `Can a power to make a statutory rule that fixes a fee be read as a power to fix it in fee units` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a power to make a statutory rule that fixes a fee be read as a power to fix it in fee units` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:82 | (1A) A provision in an Act or a statutory rule authorising an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument that prescribes, fixes or charges a fee (however expressed) may be construed as authorising the instrument maker to make a legislative instrument to prescribe, fix or charge that fee by reference to a fee unit.
-- A provision in an Act or a statutory rule authorising an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument that charges a fee.
#ASSERT `Can a power to make a legislative instrument that fixes a fee be read as a power to fix it in fee units` `a statutory rule` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a power to make a legislative instrument that fixes a fee be read as a power to fix it in fee units` `a legislative instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:83 | (2) A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes a penalty for an offence against the statutory rule (however expressed) may be construed as authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule to prescribe that penalty by reference to a penalty unit.
-- A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes a penalty for an offence against it.
#ASSERT `Can a power to make a statutory rule that fixes a penalty be read as a power to fix it in penalty units` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a power to make a statutory rule that fixes a penalty be read as a power to fix it in penalty units` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulations that convert amounts to units (s 9)`

-- src:95 | (a) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(a)—
-- src:96 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or
-- src:97 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- A fee of 125 dollars converted by a regulation taking effect on 1 July 2004: 12.5 fee units (125 divided by 10).
#ASSERT `How many fee units is a fee in dollars when a regulation converts it` 125 (Date 1 7 2004) 12.5 EQUALS JUST 12.5
-- Taking effect on 2 July 2004, with a fee unit worth 12.5 dollars: 10 fee units.
#ASSERT `How many fee units is a fee in dollars when a regulation converts it` 125 (Date 2 7 2004) 12.5 EQUALS JUST 10
-- A fee unit worth 0 divides nothing.
#ASSERT `How many fee units is a fee in dollars when a regulation converts it` 125 (Date 2 7 2004) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:98 | (b) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:99 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by $100; or
-- src:100 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- A penalty of 250 dollars converted by a regulation taking effect on 1 July 2004: 2.5 penalty units (250 divided by 100).
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty in dollars when a regulation converts it` 250 (Date 1 7 2004) 125 EQUALS JUST 2.5
-- Taking effect on 2 July 2004, with a penalty unit worth 125 dollars: 2 penalty units.
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty in dollars when a regulation converts it` 250 (Date 2 7 2004) 125 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `How many penalty units is a penalty in dollars when a regulation converts it` 250 (Date 2 7 2004) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:107 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)(a) and (b), in calculating the number of fee units or penalty units, the number of fee units or penalty units is deemed to be calculated in accordance with those provisions if the fee unit or penalty unit is rounded up to the next 2 decimal places.
-- 3.456 units rounded up to the next 2 decimal places: 3.46. A number with 2 decimal places stays as it is.
#ASSERT `What is a number of units rounded up to the next 2 decimal places` 3.456 EQUALS 3.46
#ASSERT `What is a number of units rounded up to the next 2 decimal places` 2.5 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `What is a number of units rounded up to the next 2 decimal places` 3.4601 EQUALS 3.47

§ `Notice of the dollar amounts (s 10)`

-- src:113 | (1) The Minister responsible for administering an Act or a statutory rule that provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of those fees and penalties calculated in accordance with section 7 are notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected by the fee or penalty.
-- An Act that provides for fees by fee units: the Minister who administers it must take reasonable steps.
#ASSERT `Must the Minister who administers the instrument take reasonable steps to have the dollar amounts notified` `an Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A legislative instrument, or an Act that does not provide for units: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Must the Minister who administers the instrument take reasonable steps to have the dollar amounts notified` `a legislative instrument` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must the Minister who administers the instrument take reasonable steps to have the dollar amounts notified` `an Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:115 | (2) The Minister responsible for administering an Act or a statutory rule under which a legislative instrument is made that provides for fees by fee units must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of those fees calculated in accordance with section 7 are notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected by the fee.
-- A statutory rule under which a legislative instrument is made that provides for fees by fee units.
#ASSERT `Must the Minister who administers the instrument take reasonable steps to have the dollar amounts of fees in a legislative instrument notified` `a statutory rule` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Minister who administers the instrument take reasonable steps to have the dollar amounts of fees in a legislative instrument notified` `a statutory rule` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `The Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 (s 12)`

-- src:127 | Nothing in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 applies to the fixing of—
-- src:128 | (a) a fee or penalty unit in accordance with section 5 or 11; or
-- src:129 | (b) an annual rate in accordance with section 5 or 11.
-- Fixing a fee unit under section 5: the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 does not apply.
#ASSERT `Does the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 apply to the fixing of a unit or an annual rate` `a fee unit` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 apply to the fixing of a unit or an annual rate` `an annual rate` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A fixing not under section 5 or 11, or of something else: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Does the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 apply to the fixing of a unit or an annual rate` `a fee unit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 apply to the fixing of a unit or an annual rate` `something else` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
